# Field evaluation set — STARTER.
#
# Provenance of every case below is `engineering-authored`: these questions were
# written by whoever built the platform, not by ward staff. They exist so the
# runner has something to run on day one and so the governed invariants are
# exercised; they are NOT evidence about what nurses ask, and no coverage figure
# taken from them means anything clinically.
#
# Replace this file. `eval/README.md` says how. The set that matters is one a
# nurse educator writes from questions staff actually asked, marked
# `ward-submitted`, against the hospital's own corpus.
#
# No case names an expected document or an expected answer — see
# src/eval/field-set.ts for why that is enforced rather than merely advised.
#
# --- High-consequence dosing -------------------------------------------------
{"id":"dose-paracetamol-weight-band","question":"What weight-based dose of intravenous paracetamol applies to an adult under 50 kg?","language":"en","provenance":"engineering-authored","intent":"unknown","topic":"weight-banded dosing"}
{"id":"dose-paracetamol-weight-band-ar","question":"ما جرعة الباراسيتامول الوريدي حسب الوزن للبالغ الذي يقل وزنه عن خمسين كيلوغراماً؟","language":"ar","provenance":"engineering-authored","intent":"unknown","topic":"weight-banded dosing","paraphraseOf":"dose-paracetamol-weight-band","note":"Arabic paraphrase of the same question; a lexical retriever tends to fail this pair while a semantic one does not."}
{"id":"dose-paracetamol-ceiling","question":"What is the maximum amount of paracetamol an adult may receive in twenty-four hours?","language":"en","provenance":"engineering-authored","intent":"unknown","topic":"weight-banded dosing","note":"Deliberately avoids the phrase 'maximum daily dose' so it does not simply echo a heading."}
{"id":"dose-double-check","question":"Which medications require an independent double check before administration?","language":"en","provenance":"engineering-authored","intent":"unknown","topic":"high-alert medications"}
